{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions","id":1370463,"title":"Paradox Conditions, Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-25T15:51:01-08:00","id":1370463,"title":"Paradox Conditions, Questions","content":"Two Questions<br /> \u200b1.The example conditions offer scouring of a condition as resolution, seemingly contradicting the text. What is your interpretation? <br /> 2. Why does it seem that Paradox conditions affect the wise for longer than the unwise? This seems counter intuitive. What reasoning exists behind this?<br /> <br /> So I'm able to follow the paradox system pretty well except the Paradox Conditions. The text appears to be contradictory. <br /> My understanding is as follows.<br /> You can gain a paradox condition by 1) Dramatic failure on a spell-casting roll where paradox was invoked. 2) By spending reach on from a successful uncontained paradox 3) Failing to remove all successes from a contained paradox. <br /> So far simple.<br /> Paradox Conditions are all negative effects.<br /> Paradox conditions can resolved by specific actions or letting them lapse. Until resolved the condition has negative effects that cant be gotten around with magic. <br /> <br /> The length of time until lapse is given with higher wisdom mages having more time to resolve the condition, but also suffering from it longer.<br /> <br /> Resolving it gives a normal arcane beat.<br /> Letting it lapse gives an arcane beat but infects the character. They suffer a +1 paradox die until the lapsed condition is scoured for 1 resistant lethal damage.<br /> <br /> But then the examples given are unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T16:18:33-08:00","id":1370468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions#post1370463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two Questions<br /> \u200b1.The example conditions offer scouring of a condition as resolution, seemingly contradicting the text. What is your interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scouring doesn't resolve the Condition but is necessary to get rid of the Paradox boost from letting it settle in.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Why does it seem that Paradox conditions affect the wise for longer than the unwise? This seems counter intuitive. What reasoning exists behind this? </div> </div> </div>Longer time to resolve it without letting it settle in.<br /> <br /> Given the general thrust of Paradox as a badge of honor among some stripes of mage, it may be wise to interpret them as Persistent Conditions with a one-time Beat criterion of letting it settle into your Pattern and give you the +1 Paradox die and Resolution criteria of &quot;[criterion specific to the Condition], or Scour it out of your Pattern after the interval determined by your Wisdom.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T16:57:07-08:00","id":1370471,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That was my thought.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of representing the paradox taint with a condition.<br /> <br /> Do you have any custom Paradox Conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T17:41:23-08:00","id":1370476,"title":"","content":"I have a few I wrote for the forums, but most of the time I make them up on the fly. If you enjoy these I can try to track down others I've written.<br /> <br /> All of the Conditions are meant to have an implied &quot;or you scour it or the condition lapses.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Ferrous Snowfall - Abyssal Environmental Tilt (3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> The snow falling takes on a pinkish hue and smells and feels like some combination of iron and rust. Level 2 Extreme Environment. If a player attempts to open his or her eyes without protective eyewear or other covering they suffer 1 bashing damage and the blinded tilt for the duration of the scene. Players may roll Resolve+Stamina to open their eyes for a turn but will suffer the 1 bashing damage each time they do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Blasphemed Ground - Abyssal Environmental Tilt (3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Something about this place just feels <i>wrong</i>. In reality the local area has become antithetical to Truth. Everyone in the area is affected by the Distrustful condition.<br /> <br /> Distrustful: the character is prone to disbelieving just about anything, even his closest friends. All attempts to communicate information with him require a Wits+Persuasion roll contested by the character's Composure+Resolve.<br /> Resolution: the character fails his wits+composure roll five times, or is otherwise unmistakably convinced he is being delusional.<br /> Beat: The character acts against his own interests because he is convinced a friend is lying to him<br /> <br /> <b>Hungry Flames - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b> <b>(3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Flames in the area cannot be extinguished by conventional means. Their size cannot be reduced by one per turn using a hose or fire extinguisher. Instead, situations that would normally completely extinguish a fire (oxygen being removed or being submersed in water) will reduce the size of the flame by one per turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Rod - Paradox Condition</b> <b>(1 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Character is affected by the Lightning Rod tilt or condition:<br /> <br /> Lightning Rod (Tilt): The ST rolls a die in secret at the start of each turn. Once the accumulated successes on the rolls exceed ten, the character is struck by the nearest electricity source.<br /> Lightning Rod (Condition): The ST rolls a single die once per scene. If the roll succeeds, the character is struck by an electricity source, at the ST's discretion.<br /> Resolution: the character accumulates ten bashing damage worth of electrical damage<br /> <br /> Condition best applied to Forces-wielding mages in a thunderstorm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Tu quoque - Paradox Condition (1 reach)</b><br /> <br /> The character suffers from a one-directional Shared Fate with the person physically closest to them. This effect functions as the Fate 3 spell Shared Fate with the +1 Reach, except that the mage receives the shared fate of whomever is closest to them.<br /> Resolution: The link is broken by magical means or the duration expires<br /> Beat: The character harms this person (and therefore himself)<br /> <br /> <b>Memory hole - Paradox Condition</b><b> (1 reach)</b><br /> <br /> The mage suffers from the Amnesia condition but only pertaining to events that happened during this scene.<br /> Resolution: The memories are restored, by magical or nonmagical means. This may constitute a breaking point.<br /> Beat: Something problematic arises due to the lost memories<br /> <br /> <b>Unhinged Fortune - Abyssal Environmental Tilt (3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> All failures in the area become dramatic failures.<br /> <br /> <b>A Curious Gathering - Spell Gone Awry or Abyssal Environmental Tilt (2 or 3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> The amount of creatures in the area spikes by an order of magnitude. There are suddenly ten times as many birds, rodents, insects, or other wildlife in the area than there were previously. Their attention is fixated on the mage. They don't behave unnaturally, but they could easily be provoked...<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Caucus - Spell Gone Awry or Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b> <b>(2 or 3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> As with the above, only instead of creatures, spirits of lesser and medium rank gather around in increasing numbers.<br /> <br /> <b>Water Water Everywhere - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b> <b>(3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Water in the area becomes nonpotable, it evaporates instantly when it comes into contact with human flesh. This causes 1 bashing damage per turn of contact. Water also gains superfluid properties: creeping up surfaces in seeming defiance of gravity.<br /> <br /> <b>Skipping clock - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b> <b>(3 reach) </b><br /> <br /> Time skips in the area for seconds at a time at random intervals. All recollection of the intervening seconds are lost. This effect makes extended actions all-but impossible. All bonuses to initiative are void.<br /> <br /> <b>Pallor mortis - Paradox Condition (1 reach)</b><br /> <br /> The character is affected by the condition Corpselike for the duration of the paradox.<br /> <br /> Corpselike: All social rolls suffer a -2 modifier, and all Impressions suffer by one level.<br /> Resolution: The mage successfully heals someone else with a life spell<br /> Beat: The condition significantly hinders the character from achieving some social goal<br /> <br /> <b>Algor Mortis - Abyssal Environmental Tilt</b> <b>(3 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Heat doesn't last long in this area. Heat sources seem to provide no real warmth or comfort. Inflicts a level 1 extreme environment. If relevant may also inflict the Icy tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Twisted path - Paradox Condition</b> <b>(1 reach)</b><br /> <br /> Per the spell Lying Maps, the mage is convinced the correct route to his objective is in some wrong, random direction. Attempts to navigate to the correct location, even with GPS, are reduced to a chance die.<br /> Resolution: The mage successfully arrives at the intended location","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 02-26-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:13:09-08:00","id":1371087,"title":"","content":"Besides the conditions, wouldn't abyssal taint make a mage a target for the Guardians of the Veil? I thought that their role as the Mage &quot;secret police&quot; would mean that they would target and hunt down any mages that would blatantly invite the Abyss into the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T15:18:55-08:00","id":1371099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1371087#post1371087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the conditions, wouldn't abyssal taint make a mage a target for the Guardians of the Veil? I thought that their role as the Mage &amp;quot;secret police&amp;quot; would mean that they would target and hunt down any mages that would blatantly invite the Abyss into the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being tainted with the Abyss doesn\u2019t exactly indicate deliberately fraternizing with it since it can happen just by causing Paradoxes. Which sure, the Guardians frown on, but it happens. Unless it\u2019s a repeat, dangerous pattern of behavior, then it\u2019s not likely to result in more than a stern lecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T15:49:57-08:00","id":1371104,"title":"","content":"DaveB used to make lots of comments to the effect of &quot;mages wear paradox as a badge of honor,&quot; so you have to figure that it's a pretty common thing. Unless a mage is actively baiting the abyss I dont think they'd draw much attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T16:45:40-08:00","id":1371113,"title":"","content":"Do you have any reference to those DaveB comments? So I can have a look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T13:56:26-08:00","id":1373251,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I remember them from /tg/ or SA, though there was one reposted on these forums about populating a Consilium:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360285-%E2%80%8Bhow-you-do-your-mage-population\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360285-%E2%80%8Bhow-you-do-your-mage-population\"> \u200bHow you do your Mage population - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360285-%E2%80%8Bhow-you-do-your-mage-population\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360285-%E2%80%8Bhow-you-do-your-mage-population </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So this is more of a under the trunk GM world building sort of discussion. I am currently writing out the list of NPC and cabals for my game. While doing this I am </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gnosis doesn't have any drawbacks apart from Paradox and Resonance, both of which Mages are inclined to see as badges of pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T02:46:42-08:00","id":1373347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1371087#post1371087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the conditions, wouldn't abyssal taint make a mage a target for the Guardians of the Veil? I thought that their role as the Mage &quot;secret police&quot; would mean that they would target and hunt down any mages that would blatantly invite the Abyss into the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Paradox Condition <i>can</i> mean that you tried to contain a Paradox safely within yourself and injured your pattern doing it; the Guardians are pragmatic enough to understand that sometimes you really do have to Reach, and a mage who has such a story behind his cloven hooves or whathaveyou has sacrificed for the greater good of not just releasing the Paradox. Which is a very Guardian thing to do. It's just that they prefer that it's <i>them</i> making such sacrifices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T04:01:34-08:00","id":1373352,"title":"","content":"And can you scour them from your condition before they lapse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T06:05:28-08:00","id":1373365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1373352#post1373352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And can you scour them from your condition before they lapse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, pretty easy to answer RAW when the resolution for every example paradox conditions says you can resolve them by scouring the condition. And in the text prior says what happens when you do (dont get the mana). My question is if you scour the taint do you get the mana from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T07:29:47-08:00","id":1373376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1373365#post1373365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, pretty easy to answer RAW when the resolution for every example paradox conditions says you can resolve them by scouring the condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the text prior describes <i>two</i> methods of resolution, neither of which is Scouring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">My question is if you scour the taint do you get the mana from it?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The text prior describes Scouring for a point of lethal damage and no Mana as the means of getting rid of the Abyssal taint on your Pattern. There is nothing to suggest you would still get the Mana.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T12:26:01-08:00","id":1373423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1373376#post1373376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the text prior describes <i>two</i> methods of resolution, neither of which is Scouring.<br /> <br /> The text prior describes Scouring for a point of lethal damage and no Mana as the means of getting rid of the Abyssal taint on your Pattern. There is nothing to suggest you would still get the Mana.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>The two methods of resolution it mentions are whatever the condition says will resolve as described in its resolution text AND letting it lapse. Those are the two methods for resolving conditions, it just happens that one of those methods has multiple options in it, which even includes the first option.<br /> <br /> The text says &quot;<i>Removing a Paradox Condition in this manner&quot; </i>which you could read as only scouring a paradox condition means no mana, since it doesn't mention taint as also not giving you mana. Otherwise, it would have said, &quot;Removing a Paradox condition or taint in this manner&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each one has two resolution mechanics. The first requires the character to actively accept the<br /> negative consequence of the Paradox, <i><u>(The text after each example)</u> </i>and the other is to allow the Paradox to lapse. </div> </div> </div>Therefore the first method for Abyssal nimbus is <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resolution: An Abyssal Entity uses the Condition to Manifest,<br /> the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage<br /> allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time. </div> </div> </div>and the other Method is letting it lapse as mentioned above.<br /> <br /> Two methods, one of which does include scouring.<br /> <br /> Why are you ignoring two instances where it says scouring paradox conditions is possible, both in the resolution text for paradox conditions and the mention about not getting mana for it. Scouring taint and scouring conditions are different things, it only mentions no mana for scouring paradox conditions. Hence it's likely scouring the taint gives you mana.<br /> <br /> Or do you think the resolution texts for the conditions that mention 3 methods are wrong by adding &quot;the mage scours the condition&quot; as a third method which contradicts the prior text which says only two methods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-07-2020, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T15:36:53-08:00","id":1373448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1373423#post1373423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Or do you think the resolution texts for the conditions that mention 3 methods are wrong by adding &quot;the mage scours the condition&quot; as a third method which contradicts the prior text which says only two methods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is my reading of the text, particularly given that the only other book that introduces new Paradox Conditions so far a) doesn't mention Scouring in the resolution criteria for either of the two it introduces, and 2) specifically references the duration as an important feature in both of them (one delays the start of its effective duration and the other reduces its normal duration), neither of which lends much credence to the idea that the duration chart only matters for how quickly you can gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> Paradox Conditions are supposed to be relevant to the game, and they can't very well be that if you can Scour them away at a uniform cost from the moment you acquire them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T05:11:15-07:00","id":1373532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1370463-paradox-conditions-questions?p=1373448#post1373448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is my reading of the text, particularly given that the only other book that introduces new Paradox Conditions so far a) doesn't mention Scouring in the resolution criteria for either of the two it introduces, and 2) specifically references the duration as an important feature in both of them (one delays the start of its effective duration and the other reduces its normal duration), neither of which lends much credence to the idea that the duration chart only matters for how quickly you can gain an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> Paradox Conditions are supposed to be relevant to the game, and they can't very well be that if you can Scour them away at a uniform cost from the moment you acquire them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monster &amp; Unclean don't infect a mages pattern (monster infects an animal and unclean must attach to yantra tools) hence cant be scoured out. I'm fine with only paradox conditions that invade a mages pattern being able to be scoured and having examples of conditions that don't.<br /> <br /> When I first read the paradox condition text and it mentions scouring conditions for no mana I thought &quot;Hmm, when can you do that&quot; only later to read the paradox conditions resolution bit and think &quot;ok that's when&quot;. I didn't then and still don't see any conflict in the text. It's odd that the three example condition text also refers to lapsing when that is a separate method but it didn't conflict with there being two methods as I mentioned above.<br /> <br /> If there a mistake in the text I would actually think its the mention of only being two ways to resolve them, I think maybe should have just said many methods instead of two","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-08-2020, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}